            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Both added files were reviewed in full. The validator is a local CLI with no dependencies. It makes no network calls, runs no subprocesses, and uses no eval.",
              "Input handling is bounded: skills/security-audit/validate-findings.cjs opens the file with no-follow and nonblocking flags, requires a regular file, caps size at 5 MiB, and decodes strict UTF-8. It also caps nesting depth, array length, canonical-key size, and error count.",
              "Diagnostic output is escaped for control and invisible characters, and long strings are clipped. Source paths in the findings are checked against absolute paths, traversal, backslashes, colons, and Windows reserved names.",
              "The only RegExp built from data comes from the repository's own report-schema.json, which is trusted and checked at load time. I found no reachable injection or exposure.",
              "The JSON.parse prototype-key case is handled because the code uses hasOwn checks. I found no concrete exploit path attributable to this change."
            ]
          }
        }
