            "lens": "review-resilience",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "I reviewed both new files in full for failure handling, bounded resource use, and degradation, and found no concrete production failure mode.",
              "Input handling is bounded and fails closed with a nonzero exit and a sanitized message. The limits are: a 5 MiB size cap, enforced both on fstat and while reading; no symlinks (O_NOFOLLOW); regular files only; strict UTF-8 decoding; a JSON nesting-depth limit of 64; and an array cap of 1000 items.",
              "Validation work is bounded. Canonical keys are capped at 1 MiB and the uniqueness set at 5 MiB. The error list is capped at 100 entries. Because the schema's only oneOf is at the top-level items, each of at most 1000 items is validated three times, which is cheap.",
              "Schema load errors, read errors, parse errors, and unexpected validation exceptions are each caught and reported, and each returns exit code 1. The script has no side effects such as writes or network calls, so it can be retried safely."
            ]
          }
        }
